    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0349" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Lieutenant General Alvan C. Gillem, Jr.,
                        to General Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-24">24 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In response to your request as to the method of settlement for equipment for
                    Communist Training, “War 82174” states that “Equipment transferred for Communist
                    Training will be under straight <pb facs="0350" n="338" xml:id="pg338"/>
                        Lend-Lease.”<anchor n="55" xml:id="d119-f1"/> Inquiries have been made
                    regarding where to store Communist Divisional equipment until needed.</p>
                <closer><signed>A. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gillem, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d119-f1" n="55" xml:id="d119-f1-content">
                <p>Not found in Department files; it was received at the Shanghai headquarters of
                    the U. S. Army in China on March 29.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
